#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# complex_contour_plot

#% text
# `complex_contour_plot(f, [z, z0, z1])` draws contours of a function of the complex variable `z`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A real-valued `f` (such as `abs(...)`) gives filled contours; a complex one gives the level lines of its real part and its imaginary part in two colours.

#% item
# `f == g` gives the curves where the real and the imaginary parts of `f - g` vanish.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
complex_contour_plot(abs(z^2 - 1), [z, -2 - 2*im, 2 + 2*im])
#% output
#= image("complex_contour_plot.files/complex_contour_plot-1.svgz")

#% text
# Real and imaginary parts:

#% cell
complex_contour_plot(z^2, [z, -2 - 2*im, 2 + 2*im])
#% output
#= image("complex_contour_plot.files/complex_contour_plot-2.svgz")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# An equation:

#% cell
complex_contour_plot(z^3 == 1, [z, -2 - 2*im, 2 + 2*im])
#% output
#= image("complex_contour_plot.files/complex_contour_plot-3.svgz")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `complex_plot`, `contour_plot`
